c-cbbe5d9bb642" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389923 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=[-1,0]\\times [-1,1]\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,0]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,0],\\,y\\in [-1,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}=\\{(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,1]\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/c9/c93f3ad399b88ccbaac990f8f73e93cfdcb1192f52b9b12f2d3ce178776fa13b.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in [-1,0]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}=\\{(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,1]\\}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in [-1,0],$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line segment from the point $(i,-1)$ to the point $(i,1).$\n\n![](images/65/6557201d202a401a92ee37c9a69eab9ab6ab87c6342dbb9d2afebae30141346f.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $I=[-1,0]:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following rectangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/97/97a74b119ddb8a618d6564bc077d03a5a4ceb7152702beb3682f2eab1a436b70.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389924 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389924 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389924 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389924 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389928 #edb/